QuickDict was going to be ported to a cross-platform language, but, as I
said, development ceased.

I don't even know what you mean by full text search.

Regarding fricukt, pressing enter doesn't work: I typed "gismu" into the
search bar and hit enter, nothing happened. In order to search, I have to
manually press the "sisku" button.

Also, if it's a web page, why does it need to be downloaded? Wouldn't it be
better to give it a web address? Any device which is capable of accessing it
by definition has web access, and it would be much simpler to users to
simply access that site- no need to download the latest version or
what-have-you.

Third, with the current selection of jbovalsi searching (jbovlaste,
vlasisku, even http://jbotcan.org/gismulinked.html ), what does this do that
they don't?

On Tue, Oct 11, 2011 at 10:09 AM, najrut <ruler11post@gmail.com> wrote:

> Unfortunately QuickDict had the same disadvantages as GoldenDict. Wasn't
> cross-platform, had no fulltext search.
>
